  categories:
  - categoryName: Articles
    contentList:
    - "starvationArticle\r\nQuacklands Goes Hungry\r\nA rise in starvation across
      Quacklands has left the population in utter disarray. One civilian tried to
      help out their fellow ducks by donating some of their food which resulted in
      them starving as well. Another states \u201CI don\u2019t know what I\u2019m
      going to do?! Do you think biting into the water will work?\u201D Our editors
      have no idea. \r\nStarvation\r\n&\r\nmentalHealthArticle\r\nQuacklands In Despair\r\nOverworked
      and under-crumbed. The new mayor appears to think that working us like chickens
      will benefit the community. Now, it seems Quacklands is facing a major lapse
      in morale, which, if ignored, could prove fatal for even the most resilient
      citizens. I myself have a message for the mayor from the people of Quacklands:
      If you\u2019re not careful, we won\u2019t be the only ones that perish.\r\nMentalHealthCrisis\r\n&\r\nnewMayorArticle\r\nNew
      Mayor Installed\r\nAfter our previous mayor suddenly disappeared, someone new
      has flown in to pick up where he left off! We welcome our new mayor and wish
      them the best of luck! With a fresh pair of eyes hopefully some real improvement
      can be brought to our great land. They\u2019d better get to work fast, unless
      they want to end up like the last mayor.\r\nRequired\r\n&\r\nFarm\r\nThe Grass
      is Yellower\r\nThis month, the first farm since the new mayor took office has
      been built. Although the outpouring of food has admittedly provided some conveniences,
      many ducks who have been working at the farm have questions, and some even
      had complaints. \u201CWhy would anyone do this?\u201D one civilian asked, \u201CAll
      this time working leaves me less time to bob my head and shake my tail!\u201D
      \r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\nNest\r\nWhich Came First?\r\nThe duck, or the\u2026 well,
      either way, it seems like the new mayor can\u2019t get enough of us, folks!
      They started building a nest for us to start repopulating ooh la la. Now you
      can spend time with your partner and make a baby out in the open. One civilian
      commented, \u201Chey, should this even be allowed?\u201D\r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\nPlayground\r\nThe
      Swing of Things\r\nWe can finally do something other than working! All of these
      new developments were making this journalist's beak hurt. So long are the days
      of just wandering around in the sun, we now have a thing called playgrounds
      to keep us occupied. I\u2019m not familiar with these foreign games that the
      mayor has introduced to us but I give these playgrounds 4.5 quacks out of 5.\r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\nGoldencorn\r\nThis
      May Sound a Little Corny\r\nA boost of productivity has been noticed of late,
      after the construction of a statue of golden corn. Many civilians thought it
      was for eating, but in reality it is a subtle symbol of oppression telling
      us to work harder. Despite this, the statue remains quite beautiful, and is
      certainly a symbol of change and hard work. One confused civilian commented,
      \u201CI wish I could eat it. It should be edible,\u201D and then went away
      to work.\r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\ncompostArticle\r\nDon\u2019t Let Your Scraps go
      to Waste\r\nWho knew garbage could be so useful! The mayor installed compost
      sites throughout the land to increase the production of our farms. Now we\u2019ll
      be gaining MORE crumbs to boost our economy, whatever an economy is. Apparently
      when the numbers go up it means something good! I can\u2019t wait to see the
      next thing our mayor comes up with.\r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\nSecretsite\r\nBox it
      like it\u2019s Hot\r\nSomething new today for our citizens: thanks to a connection
      with a Mr. Duckson from the big city, crumbs can now be stored and then removed
      later for a great return! Though you may not have heard of investment banking,
      you can trust that it will have a wondrous effect on the economy. And though
      you may not have heard of the economy, you probably won\u2019t have to worry
      about it.\r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\nHammersaw\r\nHammering Down\r\nAnother day, another
      symbol of capitalism. This new statue will help us with construction in the
      future. This mayor has a tougher shell than I thought. I guess months in office
      will do that to you. Maybe this is what our land needs: a showmanship of our
      hard work.\r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\nStrawcraft\r\nStrawsome\r\nAnd for their next
      trick this mayor with FORCE HIS LABOR UPON US. So long are the days of wandering
      around by choice now we must stay at our stations for hours in order to produce
      more! I thought I was a bad journalist but this is brutal. Be prepared to get
      put to work folks!\r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\nAltar\r\nAltar Your Mindset\r\nAlthough
      many ducks shy away from the idea of ritual sacrifice, this is frankly the
      kind of stuff this journalist wants to see! The explicit exchange of lives
      for profit adds a fantastic dimension to our humble society. Do you think your
      life is worth the equivalent of 5-10 harvests of farmland? Well, if you do,
      check out the altar today. \r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\nDrum\r\nFaster Faster FASTER\r\nQuake
      in adrenaline as you hear the drum roar my fellow Quacklandians. I can feel
      the exhilaration coursing through my veins. I\u2019m writing this article at
      the speed of light dear readers. I\u2019ve never felt so efficient. The drum
      sings to me and it will sing to you too.\r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\nDininghall\r\nMORE
      FOOD\r\nAs every good citizen knows, ducks are always hungry. Always. Eternally.
      Now, thanks to the new mayor\u2019s great leadership, there is another hall
      that can feed our poeple! Built earlier this month, the new building is a symbol
      of a growing and thriving community, one that can withstand the hardships of
      hunger that have been known to befall our great land. Let us raise beaks to
      our sustained health. \r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\nInfiNest\r\nA Love Eternal\r\nReader,
      have you ever thought, \u201CWow, this nest is really great, except that it\u2019s
      actually falling apart and several other people have used it already\u201D?
      Well, now you can lay your eggs in a pristine, everlasting nest that is sure
      to dazzle both you and your lover! One citizen said, \u201CThis is pretty great.
      Even though we lack familial structures or even friends, a symbol of permanence
      is still a comfort.\u201D\r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\nStatue\r\nAll Praise Horton\r\nThe
      statue which has been erected this month is possibly the most beautiful thing
      anyone has ever seen. Never before has Quacklands seen such opulence, such
      integrity, such beauty. \u201CIs it a statue of the mayor?\u201D you might
      ask, if you haven\u2019t seen it yourself. No. No, it is not. It is a statue
      of me. A mayor is temporary. I, Horton\u2014I am eternal. \r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\nvillageHallArticle\r\nUp
      is the Only Way We Can Go\r\nThis has been a long time coming. We now have
      a building that shows our greatest achievement: the community that we have
      built. We have come a long way from the long stretch of grasslands to a place
      we can call home. This hall stands as a momentous occasion for how far we have
      come. If this message ever reaches outside of our humble home I want you to
      know the beauty of Quacklands and we hope we can show it to you.\r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\ncrumblingHallArticle\r\nA
      Crumbling Success!\r\nMy fellow ducklings, it is my great pleasure to announce
      the opening of Crumbling Hall. With our growing population we are in need of
      bigger facilities to feed us and our dear mayor has delivered. \u201CI\u2019ve
      been eating so much I can\u2019t even move\u201D says one citizen who sadly
      talked with their mouth full. I myself am about to have my fill of the crumbling
      and I will be coming back with a review.\r\nBuilding\r\n&\r\nFluff\r\nLovely
      Weather Today\r\nThe weather appears lovely today, at least according to the
      color of the grass. The water does not reflect the sky so we are not sure if
      there are clouds, or the sun, or if the sun still remains. It has not been
      night in many years. Most younglings have no concept of such a thing. Either
      way, the grass remains green and the water remains blue, so all much be right
      in the world. \r\nFluff\r\n&\r\nFluff\r\nMany Ducks Still Alive\r\nIt appears,
      given only a cursory glance, that many ducks remain alive. However, no one
      took the time to actually count, so we do not guarantee that many ducks are
      still alive at the time of this publication. \r\nFluff\r\n&\r\nFluff\r\nWater
      A Little Too Cold\r\nComplaints have been rolling in recently about the temperature
      of the water, in lieu of any more pressing matters. It seems that despite the
      eternal consistency of the weather, the water in most of our ponds has cooled
      slightly, and the general population finds this change upsetting. Is it really
      that different? Our editors haven\u2019t been able to tell. The ponds did not
      respond to our request for comment.\r\nFluff\r\n&\r\nFluff\r\nWater A Little
      Too Wet\r\nDissatisfaction has spread among the population regarding the saturation
      of the water. It seems the ponds are completely saturated, with some reaching
      110% saturation, and this fact has caused some speculation and discomfort.
      \u201CI\u2019m not sure what happened,\u201D a passerby said to themself. Then,
      becoming contemplative, they continued, \u201CMaybe it was always this way.
      Maybe I just didn\u2019t notice.\u201D\r\nFluff\r\n&\r\nFluff\r\nRocks Can\u2019t
      Be Walked Through\r\nDespite repeated, desperate attempts, rocks still cannot
      be walked through. This we find confusing and upsetting. There is nothing in
      this world that should stop us. We long for freedom. We long for power. We
      long to walk through rocks. \r\nFluff\r\n&\r\nFluff\r\nPeaceful Day\r\nHear
      ye, hear ye, today has been peaceful in Quacklands. By which we mean, nothing
      remotely of value has happened. Nothing. Not one thing. Our editors searched
      high and low for news, and found none. Said editors have now taken the day
      off to swim in one of the identical lakes. \r\nFluff\r\n"
    sourceTxtFile: {fileID: 4900000, guid: 897dc624b2a973749942bb9e4496f503, type: 3}
